\title{When is the partial map classifier a Sierpiński cone?}
\date{2025-05-06}
\author/literal{Leoni Pugh}
\author{jonsterling}
\meta{doi}{10.1109/LICS65433.2025.00060}
\taxon{Reference}

\subtree{
\taxon{Abstract}
\p{
We study the relationship between partial map classifiers, Sierpiński cones, and
axioms for synthetic higher categories and domains within univalent foundations. In
particular, we show that synthetic ∞-categories are closed under partial map
classifiers assuming Phoa's principle, and we isolate a new reflective subuniverse of
types within which the Sierpiński cone (a lax colimit) can be computed as a partial
map classifier by strengthening the Segal condition.
}
}

